# The mob editor (olc.c's medit and do_medit, olc_act.c's medit_*) and the mob program editor (olc_mpcode.c), with
# Planner (security 9) in Midgaard, and Delver (security 0). The string editor's "@" is sent as "x", a backspace,
# "@" (see redit.scn).
# - medit with no vnum, a bad one, create's refusals (its area message says "OEdit"); edit mobile 3062 (fido)
# - every field: name, short, long, desc, level, alignment, hitroll, wealth, damtype, group (and group show), sex,
#   act (ACT_IS_NPC stays), affect, armor (one to four values), form, parts, imm, res, vuln, material, off,
#   size, the three dice (cut at non-digits), race (its flags added), position, spec; each refusal
# - shop: every subcommand, before and after assign, and remove
# - mpedit: create (and its refusals), show, list, code in the string editor, create from inside; addmprog
#   (its phrase is one lower-cased word) and delmprog (which clears the trigger's bit); changing a program's
#   code tells each mob using it ("Editting mob"), and a fido loaded then answers "hello" with the new code;
#   deleting one of two speech programs clears the speech bit, so the other no longer answers "bark"
# - mpedit list: newest first, and not the program at the area's first vnum (ENTRE is strict)
# - medit create 3013; the room editor's mshow; asave changed saves Midgaard; the prompt's %o and %O
# - Delver can't edit or create mobs or programs, and nor can a mob
@connect b
Planner
smoke123
@return
@return
scroll 0
goto 3001
force hassan medit 3062
